  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "P.S.Mahapatra vs S.Baskaran on 14 June, 2018 Author: P.N.Prakash Bench: P.N.Prakash In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 14.06.2018 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice P.N.Prakash Crl.O.P.No.10640 of 2018 and Crl.M.P.Nos.5456 and 5457 of 2018 P.S.Mahapatra .. Petitioner Vs S.Baskaran The Food Safety Officer Wallajahpet District Vellore.",
    "facts": "2. On 24.06.2015, the Food Safety Officer inspected the shop of Thangaraj [A2] at 77/15 Main Road, Walajapet and lifted TATA Tea Chakra Gold samples in accordance with the Food Safety and Standards Act and sent the same to the State Food Analysis Laboratory, Guindy for analysis and report. The report of the Analyst showed that the sample was adulterated. After obtaining the Analyst Report, the officials sent a copy of the same to the TATA Global Beverages Limited, Tumkur Road, Bengaluru Rural District, Karnataka, on the premise that they had manufactured the product. The petitioner, who was the Chief Manager (Legal) of the TATA Global Beverages Limited opted for sending the sample to the Central Food Laboratory (Referral Laboratory) in Kolkata. The report received from the Central Food Laboratory confirmed the report of the State Food Analysis P.S.Mahapatra vs S.Baskaran on 14 June, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/42473484/ 1 Laboratory and therefore, a prosecution has been launched in STC No.208 of 2016 before the Judicial Magistrate No.II, Walajapet against the petitioner herein and Thangaraj, for quashing which, the petitioner is before this Court.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that the petitioner was working as the Chief Manager (Legal) in the TATA Global Beverages Limited and that he was neither the Managing Director or Director of the Company. He further submitted that on his advice as Chief Manager (Legal,) the second sample was sent to the Referral Laboratory for analysis and therefore, he cannot be mulcted with criminal liability. 6. The prosecution fairly admitted that Mahapatra, the petitioner herein, was working as Chief Manager (Legal) in TATA Global Beverages Limited and that he is not a person who has been nominated by the Company in terms of Section 66 of the Food Safety and Standards Act by the State authorities. 7. Learned Government Advocate (Crl.Side) submitted that the authorities sent a communication to TATA Global Beverages Limited asking them to disclose the person who was nominated by them and since there was no response from the Company, the prosecution has been launched against the Company, making the petitioner to represent the Company.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that the petitioner was working as the Chief Manager (Legal) in the TATA Global Beverages Limited and that he was neither the Managing Director or Director of the Company. He further submitted that on his advice as Chief Manager (Legal,) the second sample was sent to the Referral Laboratory for analysis and therefore, he cannot be mulcted with criminal liability. 6. The prosecution fairly admitted that Mahapatra, the petitioner herein, was working as Chief Manager (Legal) in TATA Global Beverages Limited and that he is not a person who has been nominated by the Company in terms of Section 66 of the Food Safety and Standards Act by the State authorities. 7. Learned Government Advocate (Crl.Side) submitted that the authorities sent a communication to TATA Global Beverages Limited asking them to disclose the person who was nominated by them and since there was no response from the Company, the prosecution has been launched against the Company, making the petitioner to represent the Company.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
